00:26:16.860 --> 00:26:17.546
FENG LU: Right.

00:26:17.546 --> 00:26:19.420
The other thing I also
want to highlight here

00:26:19.420 --> 00:26:22.450
is in our GA release,
Cloud Composer

00:26:22.450 --> 00:26:24.760
starts to support a
KubernetesPodOperator.

00:26:24.760 --> 00:26:27.610
What that gives to you is
the flexibility for you

00:26:27.610 --> 00:26:33.640
to start and run any container
within Cloud Composer.

00:26:33.640 --> 00:26:35.570
We, for example in the past--

00:26:35.570 --> 00:26:39.200
Tom, you probably also got
a lot of similar questions.

00:26:39.200 --> 00:26:42.460
Like, people ask, hey, I have
this dependency that is not

00:26:42.460 --> 00:26:46.910
really [INAUDIBLE] dependency,
how should I install and import

00:26:46.910 --> 00:26:48.950
that dependency into Composer?

00:26:48.950 --> 00:26:49.700
TOM MCGRATH: Yeah.

00:26:49.700 --> 00:26:52.650
That's a common question--
how to configure, customize,

00:26:52.650 --> 00:26:54.405
add in some custom
code, et cetera.

00:26:54.405 --> 00:26:55.030
FENG LU: Right.

00:26:55.030 --> 00:26:57.880
Now, as things become
so easy, anything

00:26:57.880 --> 00:27:01.170
you need to do that Composer
doesn't provide to you out

00:27:01.170 --> 00:27:04.600
of the box, just go
and create a container,

00:27:04.600 --> 00:27:08.092
and then bring that container
to Workflow, to Composer.

00:27:08.092 --> 00:27:09.050
TOM MCGRATH: Very nice.

