we have discussed in the demo.

00:31:40.110 --> 00:31:42.300
We have created a composing
environment-- walks you

00:31:42.300 --> 00:31:45.430
through the various
configuration options.

00:31:45.430 --> 00:31:49.110
We have also shown you how you
could inspect your workflows

00:31:49.110 --> 00:31:51.870
in Airflow web UI, and then
some of the common tasks

00:31:51.870 --> 00:31:54.360
you could perform
using Airflow web UI,

00:31:54.360 --> 00:31:58.610
like triggering a DAG run,
inspecting log details.

00:31:58.610 --> 00:32:01.540
And then sometimes, if you
need to get a little bit more

00:32:01.540 --> 00:32:04.740
debugging with [INAUDIBLE]
Stackdriver as well,

00:32:04.740 --> 00:32:06.130
you can get those information.

00:32:06.130 --> 00:32:06.880
TOM MCGRATH: Yeah.

00:32:06.880 --> 00:32:09.070
I can definitely see
how, through this demo,

00:32:09.070 --> 00:32:11.000
we are definitely taking
care of and meeting

00:32:11.000 --> 00:32:13.430
a lot of those challenges
that we talked about earlier.

00:32:13.430 --> 00:32:14.055
FENG LU: Right.

00:32:16.280 --> 00:32:19.300
So earlier, we mentioned that
the way how Airflow [INAUDIBLE]

00:32:19.300 --> 00:32:21.110
DAGs is really code.

00:32:21.110 --> 00:32:24.080
So with code, it opens up a
lot of possibilities for you

